hostname receiver
!
ip routing
!
interface Loopback0
   ip address 10.0.0.3/32
!
interface Ethernet1
   description to aggregator:eth2
   no switchport
   ip address 10.1.23.2/30
!
! ============================================================
! YOUR TASKS ON RECEIVER
! ============================================================
!
! TASK 1 — Base BGP
!   configure
!   router bgp 65003
!      bgp router-id 10.0.0.3
!      neighbor 10.1.23.1 remote-as 65002
!      !
!      address-family ipv4
!         neighbor 10.1.23.1 activate
!         network 10.0.0.3/32
!      !
!
! TASK 2 — Observe BGP table before aggregation
!   show bgp ipv4 unicast
!   Expected (no aggregate configured):
!     10.0.0.1/32
!     10.0.0.2/32
!     10.0.0.3/32
!     10.1.1.0/24
!     10.1.2.0/24
!     10.1.3.0/24
!     10.1.4.0/24
!
! TASK 3 — Observe BGP table with basic aggregate (summary + specifics)
!   After aggregator configures: aggregate-address 10.1.0.0/22
!   show bgp ipv4 unicast
!   Expected: 10.1.0.0/22 ADDED, four /24s still present
!
!   show bgp ipv4 unicast 10.1.0.0/22
!   Look for the "Atomic Aggregate" attribute.
!   The AS-path for 10.1.0.0/22 is empty (aggregator claims it as local).
!
! TASK 4 — Observe BGP table with summary-only
!   After aggregator configures: aggregate-address 10.1.0.0/22 summary-only
!   show bgp ipv4 unicast
!   Expected: ONLY 10.1.0.0/22 — four /24s are GONE
!
!   This is the desired production behavior: receiver only sees the summary.
!   If 10.1.3.0/24 specifically goes down on originator, receiver doesn't know —
!   it just knows 10.1.0.0/22 is reachable. Some traffic may black-hole
!   if the aggregator can't reach the specific subnet.
!
! TASK 5 — Observe AS-path with as-set
!   After aggregator configures: aggregate-address 10.1.0.0/22 summary-only as-set
!   show bgp ipv4 unicast 10.1.0.0/22
!
!   AS-path should show: {65001}
!   The curly braces { } indicate an AS-set (unordered set of ASNs).
!   This tells receiver that AS65001 contributed to this aggregate.
!   The atomic-aggregate attribute disappears when as-set is used.
!
! TASK 6 — Verify reachability
!   ping 10.1.1.1     (should reach originator's Loopback1)
!   ping 10.0.0.1     (should reach originator's Loopback0)
!   These pings work because aggregator has more-specific routes for forwarding.
! ============================================================
end
